## Authority and boundary

This is the operator-approved semantic contract. `AUTHORITY.md` is incorporated
verbatim by reference (SHA-256 `<computed-by-rehash>`). No research agent may add
binding scope or redefine DONE.

## Dependencies

- None, unless this topic genuinely cannot produce a result without another topic's
  completed output. List that topic's exact id here if so -- never for scheduling
  preference (see docs/topic-authoring.md's dependency-vs-order distinction).

## Approved finite obligations

- **SCOPE-01** — <first checkable point, from AUTHORITY.md's scope section>
- **SCOPE-02** — <second checkable point>
- <...>

## Required deliverables

- **TOPIC-SYNTHESIS** — Topic-specific synthesis with one section per approved obligation (`SYNTHESIS.md`).

## Semantic exit condition

Continue until every obligation above has a terminal disposition (supported,
contradicted, unresolved, or deferred), pending evidence and contradictions are
dispositioned, and every deliverable exists. `chassis/semantic-state.py validate` is
the executable gate — not a description of it. No fixed iteration, token, source, or
time limit defines DONE.

## Storage

This topic's own ledgers in this directory. No external storage is required. If you
configure one (a vector index, a graph database, whatever fits your domain), name the
exact binding here — never assume one exists just because another topic uses one.
